  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A Wire Contour has a new per-operation option: `sharp_corners`. The default is off.\n- Off: the behaviour does not change. A sharp inside corner is refused by name, as before.\n- On: the cover law accepts an uncut rest up to the kerf offset (wire radius + spark gap). A sharp inside corner of 60 degrees or more keeps no more than that.\n- The worst accepted rest is a note on the path (`wire EDM: sharp inside corners stated - ...`).\n- The post's wire verify line also says the note. It is not a refusal.\n- A rest past the kerf offset is still refused. The message says that the option was on.\n- The option is in these places:\n  - the project file (`sharp_corners`, absent when off, so old files read unchanged);\n  - the wire page, Geometry tab (\"Sharp inside corners at the wire radius\"), applied by `EditOperationParams`;\n  - MCP `edit_operation`, through the params DTO (no new tool is necessary).\n- The 4-axis cut does not read the option. It keeps its own `heal_tolerance`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe cover law in `motion::wire_edm::laws` had one rule: each profile point must be within the kerf offset of the wire path. A sharp inside corner always breaks that rule. The report's known-good Sodick program cuts a sharp 10 mm square, and the corner takes the wire radius.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `motion` lib `wire_edm::sharp_tests::a_sharp_square_die_is_cut_when_sharp_inside_corners_are_stated`: a sharp 10 mm square die with k = 0.162 mm. Off is refused with the issue's numbers (0.1620, 0.0671). On is cut, with the note and rest 0.0671. The wire corner stays k from both sides. A punch gets no note.\n- `motion` lib `wire_edm::sharp_tests::an_inside_corner_past_the_wire_radius_stays_refused`: a 30-degree corner stays refused with the option on.\n- `app` `wire_sharp_corners::a_sharp_square_die_is_cut_and_verified_with_its_corner_rest_as_a_note`: the command path, generation, the verify line, the project round trip, and undo.\n- `ui` lib `wire_page_tests::wire_sharp_inside_corners_toggle_applies_and_undoes`: the checkbox, Apply and undo.\n- `motion` lib `wire_edm::sharp_tests::a_tapered_sharp_square_die_keeps_its_corner_rest_note` (review fix): a sharp square die with a 1-degree taper keeps the corner-rest note. The note names the top plane and the kerf across the leaning wire.\n- `app` `wire_sharp_corners::a_tapered_sharp_square_die_says_its_corner_rest_on_the_verify_line` (review fix): a tapered sharp die generates, verifies with no problem, and the verify line says the rest.\n- Mutation (review fix): the taper drops the carried note. The two tapered pins are red. After the restore, they are green.\n- Red before the fix: the pins did not compile (the option did not exist). On unchanged code, the sharp die is refused (the existing test `a_corner_tighter_than_the_wire_is_refused_by_name` pins that).\n- Mutation checks (each red, then green after the restore):\n  - `sharp_reach` gives 0 when the option is on (the old law): `a_sharp_square_die_is_cut_when_sharp_inside_corners_are_stated` is red.\n  - `sharp_reach` has no bound (1e9): `an_inside_corner_past_the_wire_radius_stays_refused` is red.\n  - The verify line does not add the note: `a_sharp_square_die_is_cut_and_verified_with_its_corner_rest_as_a_note` is red.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`) on head c66edc9ef (merged with upstream main 69c9fd7af): 651 steps, 1 failed. The failure is `example_catalog` `catalog_2d_adaptive_pocket::{rebuilds,regenerates}`, which passed the 60 s timer limit under a machine load near 50. This change does not touch that code. Alone, the two tests pass in 36 s.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` on c66edc9ef: clean.\n\n## Heavy and light lanes (head c66edc9ef)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: the `motion heavy` and `app heavy` lanes, 241 steps, 0 failed, 103.8 min. Six known-fail tests are red as expected (#1950, #2849).\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 3 steps, 0 failed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe wire page, Geometry tab. After the change, the page has the new row \"Sharp inside corners at the wire radius\". The default is off.\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3232/before-geometry.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3232/after-geometry.png) |\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.cl` or `.nc` file changed. The other test changes add `sharp_corners: false` to struct literals only.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The open run's own mitre-fold check (`open::offset`) does not change. An open run with a very short segment at a sharp corner can still be refused there.\n- The 4-axis cut ignores the option.\n- On a tapered cut, the rest is measured on the top plane, where the cover law runs. The note says so. The lower plane has no separate rest reading.\n- No run on a real control.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- The open draft chain #2972, #2974, #2978, #2979, #2981, #2992, #2993 and #2999 adds other fields to the same `WireContourOp` literals in `crates/app/tests/*` and `wire_edm_dto.rs`. It touches the same files, but different fields. Whichever merges second refreshes. Each conflict is two added lines.\n- #3205 and #3219 touch `wire_verify.rs`, in different functions.\n- #3058 touches `open.rs`, in different functions.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3207-wire-sharp-corners.md`.\n\nChangelog: Wire Contour can accept sharp inside corners at the wire radius (new per-operation option, default off); the corner leftover is said as a note in the path and the verify line.\n\nFixes #3207\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
